  "synthesis_conclusions": [
    "Haptic displays are crucial for enhancing realism and immersion in virtual environments, offering exciting applications in medicine, entertainment, education, industry, and graphic arts.",
    "The human haptic system's capabilities (tactile spatial and vibration resolution, kinesthetic resolution, force control precision, and perceptual resolution for stiffness) define the performance specifications for haptic interfaces.",
    "Computer haptics has advanced significantly in rendering virtual object shapes, textures, and friction, utilizing techniques like force shading, force perturbation, and displacement mapping to improve realism.",
    "Multimodal integration of visual, haptic, and auditory sensory information is essential for immersive virtual worlds, with visual cues often dominating haptic perception.",
    "Skewing the relationships between haptic and other sensory displays can effectively expand the perceived range of object properties in virtual environments.",
    "Haptics is being successfully integrated into distributed virtual environments, enabling web-based perceptual experiments and extensions to VRML."
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "Haptic interface devices need significant improvements in range, resolution, bandwidth, and torque displays, as well as the development of devices for multi-finger tasks, large workspaces, and sophisticated tactile displays (including temperature stimuli).",
    "Computer haptics requires more realistic and computationally efficient models for deformable objects and parametric surfaces, better synchronization of multimodal displays, and standardized protocols for haptics in distributed virtual environments.",
    "A deeper understanding of human abilities and limitations in virtual environments is necessary, requiring more human studies to inform the design of future VE systems."
  ],
